```lean
lemma heatKernelSpatial_contDiff_compat (n : ℕ) :
    ContDiff ℝ (⊤ : ℕ∞) (heatKernelSpatial n 1) := by
  -- heatKernelSpatial n 1 = (4π*1)^... * exp(...)
  change ContDiff ℝ (⊤ : ℕ∞) (fun x : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) => (4 * Real.pi * 1) ^ (-(n : ℝ) / 2) * Real.exp (-‖x‖ ^ 2 / (4 * 1)))
```
Hmm the change with *1 forms — the change target must be defeq to the goal — `heatKernelSpatial n 1` unfolds to `fun x => (4 * Real.pi * 1) ^ (-(n : ℝ) / 2) * Real.exp (-‖x‖ ^ 2 / (4 * 1))` — so change to exactly that:
```lean
  change ContDiff ℝ (⊤ : ℕ∞)
    (fun x : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) => (4 * Real.pi * 1) ^ (-(n : ℝ) / 2) * Real.exp (-‖x‖ ^ 2 / (4 * 1)))
  exact ((contDiff_const : ContDiff ℝ (⊤ : ℕ∞) (fun _ : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) => (4 * Real.pi * 1) ^ (-(n : ℝ) / 2))).mul
    (Real.contDiff_exp.comp (((contDiff_norm_sq ℝ (E := EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)) :
      ContDiff ℝ (⊤ : ℕ∞) (fun x : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) => ‖x‖ ^ 2)).neg.div_const (4 * 1)))))
```
The `.div_const (4*1)` gives `fun x => -‖x‖²/(4*1)` — matching the goal exactly. `ContDiff.mul`, `Real.contDiff_exp`, `contDiff_const`. This avoids the *1 mismatch entirely by using `4 * 1` consistently. And in Audit, use `(Evans.heatKernelSpatial_contDiff_compat n).continuous`.

